    "summary": "The drawer and spike can't share a corner: the configurator refused it, so this is a compromise. Both parts are on cell 0,0, but at different corners, and they don't touch.\n\n- **Drawer:** on cell 0,0, which is now a north half base. The drawer sits on its south cut face.\n- **What I tried:** the only spike spot next to the drawer was cell 0,0's east corner, where the drawer's face ends. The configurator refused a spike there (SPIKE_CLASH) because the drawer fills that corner.\n- **What I built instead:** I added a base at 0,-1 so a spike could stand at cell 0,0's north-east corner. There are four bases in all.\n- **Finishing:** I capped the open faces and bolted the joints. The build check found no issues and no mesh collisions.",
